# OAuth client ID (type "Web application") from the Google Cloud Console. It
# is what lets Configurações → Backup send the backup to the user's own Google
# Drive (hidden appDataFolder). Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill it in.
#
# Not a secret: the implicit OAuth flow puts it in the bundle by design. But it
# IS an identity — Drive's appDataFolder is per client ID, so a different id
# hides every backup users already made. Never rotate it casually, and keep the
# GitHub repository variable GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml)
# equal to the one used in development.
#
# Leave it empty and the Drive group says the account is not configured in
# this build; everything else in the app works as before.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

123456789012-abc123def456.apps.googleusercontent.com